{
  "_comment": [
    "Cross-language conformance suite. The TypeScript reader and the Python reader",
    "both execute every case here and must produce identical outcomes.",
    "",
    "This is the guarantee that the two implementations cannot drift. A change to",
    "one language's gate logic that is not mirrored in the other fails here, in",
    "both test suites, immediately.",
    "",
    "'registry: constants' cases run against data/constants.json \u2014 the real data.",
    "'registry: fixtures' cases run against the synthetic entries below, which exist",
    "because every real entry is currently unverified and so cannot exercise the",
    "happy path."
  ],
